enFacet by providing similar functionality for closing trades      Improves UX by allowing atomic execution of multi-step processes and removing the need for direct      blockchain interaction from the trading parties","kind":"dev","methods":{"instantCancelCloseIntent((address,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes,(address,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes)":{"details":"Combines the cancel request from PartyA and acceptance from PartyB (if needed otherwise the second signature can be empty)\t    into a single atomic transaction      May result in either EXPIRED or CANCELED status depending on the intent's deadline","params":{"partyASignature":"Cryptographic signature from PartyA authorizing the cancellation","partyBSignature":"Cryptographic signature from PartyB authorizing the acceptance","signedAcceptCancelCloseIntent":"The intent data for PartyB's acceptance of the cancellation","signedCancelCloseIntent":"The intent data for PartyA's cancellation request"}},"instantCreateAndFillCloseIntent((address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes,(address,bytes32,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes)":{"details":"Combines PartyA's request to close a trade and PartyB's filling it into one operation      Verifies signatures from both parties before creating and executing the close      This atomic operation eliminates the typical multi-step process and reduces gas costs","params":{"partyASignature":"Cryptographic signature from PartyA authorizing intent creation","partyBSignature":"Cryptographic signature from PartyB authorizing the fill","signedCloseIntent":"The complete close intent data structure from PartyA","signedFillCloseIntent":"The fill parameters from PartyB (price and quantity)"}},"instantFillCloseIntent((address,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes)":{"details":"Allows any third party to fill a close intent using PartyB's signed authorization      Verifies the signature before executing the close at the specified price and quantity      This function is